# Ant Design 6 Drawer sizing

In Ant Design 6, Drawer `width` and `height` are **deprecated**. Use `size` instead.

## Rules

- Prefer the shared wrapper: `import { Drawer } from '@/components'` (or `@/components/drawer`).
- Always pass **`size`**, never `width` / `height`, on Drawer.
- `size` accepts a number (px), CSS string (`'50%'`, `'100vw'`), or preset (`'default'` | `'large'`).
- Do **not** import `Drawer` from `antd` directly in app screens unless there is a strong reason; the shared wrapper maps legacy `width`/`height` → `size` as a safety net, but call sites must still use `size`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Drawer width={980} open={open} onClose={onClose} />
<Drawer height={400} placement="top" />

// ✅ GOOD
<Drawer size={980} open={open} onClose={onClose} />
<Drawer size={400} placement="top" />
<Drawer size="100vw" open={open} onClose={onClose} />
```

## Related Ant Design 6 notes

- `InputNumber` `addonBefore` / `addonAfter` → wrap with `Space.Compact` instead.
- Prefer `Space orientation="vertical"` (antd 6) over deprecated `direction` where this codebase already uses `orientation`.
